\section{Technical Field}
The present invention relates to high-performance simulation systems for modeling
kinetic, biomechanical, and environmental dynamics in professional sports.
More specifically, the invention integrates Major League Baseball (MLB) Statcast
telemetry, astrophysical entropy sources, and post-quantum cryptographic
verification into a unified simulation architecture.

\section{Background}
Conventional baseball simulation engines rely on deterministic physics
approximations and limited environmental modeling. Existing systems do not
incorporate universe-scale entropy sources, cryptographically verifiable state
transitions, multi-domain tensor evolution, or autonomous zero-knowledge proof
validation. No prior art discloses a simulation engine that binds real-time MLB
telemetry with cosmic entropy and Ring-LWE lattice commitments.

\section{Summary of the Invention}
The invention provides a tamper-proof, astrophysically seeded, physics-accurate
simulation engine capable of modeling baseball trajectories, player kinematics,
and environmental conditions under universe-mimetic stochastic boundaries.
The system introduces:
\begin{itemize}
